{# Liquidation Report — GAM Vol. II, Appendix 44 (checklist code LR-44): BODY.

   Held as a partial so the liquidation packet prints the same substance under
   its own cover — see `_iot45_body.html.j2` for the same note.

   The LR is a NETTING instrument, not a payment instrument. It states what was
   advanced, what was actually spent, and which of two things closes the gap: a
   refund evidenced by an official receipt (COA Circular 97-002), or a
   difference payable on a separate DV. Everything else on the page exists to
   make those three figures traceable.

   **The netting prints `advance − spent`**, which is the direction
   `services/per_diem.py::settle` computes (`diff = advance − grand`). DV-32
   prints the opposite direction because it IS the payment instrument. Putting
   the DV's sign convention on this page would give it an arithmetic that
   disagrees with the service that produced its numbers — which is exactly how
   a transcription error hides.

   **Nothing here is computed.** `to_refund` and `to_reimburse` come from
   `settle`; `refund_amount` is the figure recorded against the official
   receipt. Subtracting anything at render time would be a second, drifting
   implementation of settlement (`_dv32_body.html.j2`'s rule, restated).

   **The itinerary is deliberately absent** — that is Appendix 45, and it
   travels in the same packet. The per-DAY table stays, because it is the audit
   basis for the largest figure on the page and "why was this day paid at 50%?"
   is the first question a post-audit asks.

   **What the certification boxes may say.** `_dv32_body.html.j2`'s rule is that
   a pre-filled name in a box the system cannot enforce asserts something
   untrue. That rule is applied here with new information, not relaxed:
     A — the claimant's name prints UNDER the rule (it identifies who signs, the
         `_iot45_body.html.j2` convention). Filing IS certification A, submit is
         owner-only, so the filing timestamp is a fact the system holds.
     B — the signature line stays BLANK. The workflow records who cleared
         `certify_b` on `reimb.liquidation.certify`, so that fact is stated in a
         `note` BENEATH the box, never on the `signature-name` line: a name over
         an empty rule reads as a completed certification to anyone holding the
         page, and the ink is still required.
     C — blank, and it must stay blank forever. The workflow records the ADMIN
         OFFICER who typed the mandatory comment, NOT the Head of the Accounting
         Unit who signed on paper. Printing the recorder in box C would name the
         wrong person in a COA certification — a worse untruth than a blank box.
         The signed page is filed under checklist item CRT-C. #}
<div class="field-grid">
  <span class="field-label">Accountable officer</span>
  <span class="field-value">{{ claimant.full_name }}</span>
  <span class="field-label">Employee no.</span>
  <span class="field-value">{{ claimant.employee_no or "—" }}</span>

  <span class="field-label">Position</span>
  <span class="field-value">{{ claimant.position_title or "—" }}</span>
  <span class="field-label">Division / Section</span>
  <span class="field-value">{{ claimant.section or claimant.division or "—" }}</span>

  <span class="field-label">Serial no.</span>
  <span class="field-value">{{ claim.ref_no or "Not yet assigned" }}</span>
  <span class="field-label">Fund cluster</span>
  <span class="field-value">{{ claim.fund_source or "—" }}</span>

  <span class="field-label">Travel order</span>
  <span class="field-value">
    {{ claim.dpo_no or "—" }}
    {% if claim.dpo_date %}dated {{ claim.dpo_date | manila_date }}{% endif %}
  </span>
  <span class="field-label">Period covered</span>
  <span class="field-value">
    {{ claim.date_depart | manila_date }} – {{ claim.date_return | manila_date }}
  </span>

  <span class="field-label">Cash advance</span>
  <span class="field-value">
    {% if advance.dv_no %}
    DV {{ advance.dv_no }}
    {% else %}
    DV no. not recorded
    {% endif %}
    {% if advance.dv_date %}dated {{ advance.dv_date | manila_date }}{% endif %}
  </span>
  <span class="field-label">Liquidation due</span>
  <span class="field-value">{{ claim.liquidation_deadline | manila_date }}</span>
</div>

<h2>Purpose of travel</h2>
<p>{{ claim.purpose or "—" }}</p>
<p class="note">Destination: {{ claim.destination or "—" }}</p>

<h2>Particulars — expenses incurred</h2>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Particulars</th>
      <th class="amount">Amount</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Travelling expenses — daily travel expense (EO 77, s. 2019)</td>
      <td class="amount">{{ totals.per_diem | money }}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Travelling expenses — transportation fares</td>
      <td class="amount">{{ totals.transport | money }}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Other expenses — lodging bills, terminal fees and the like</td>
      <td class="amount">{{ totals.other | money }}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr class="total">
      <td>Total amount spent</td>
      <td class="amount">{{ totals.grand | money }}</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

{% if totals.days %}
<h2>Basis of the daily travel expense</h2>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Date</th>
      <th>Day</th>
      <th>Region / cluster</th>
      <th class="amount">Daily rate</th>
      <th class="amount">%</th>
      <th class="amount">Amount</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% for day in totals.days %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ day.date | manila_date }}</td>
      <td>{{ day.day_type or "—" }}</td>
      <td>
        {{ day.region_code or "—" }}
        {% if day.cluster %}/ {{ day.cluster }}{% endif %}
      </td>
      <td class="amount">{{ day.daily_rate | money }}</td>
      <td class="amount">{{ day.pct if day.pct is not none else "—" }}</td>
      <td class="amount">{{ day.amount | money }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
    <tr class="total">
      <td colspan="5">Total daily travel expense</td>
      <td class="amount">{{ totals.per_diem | money }}</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
{% endif %}

<h2>Settlement of the cash advance</h2>
<table>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>
        Amount of cash advance received
        {% if advance.dv_no %}
        (per DV {{ advance.dv_no }}{% if advance.dv_date %},
        dated {{ advance.dv_date | manila_date }}{% endif %})
        {% endif %}
      </td>
      <td class="amount">{{ totals.advance | money }}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Less: total amount spent</td>
      <td class="amount">({{ totals.grand | money }})</td>
    </tr>
    <tr class="total">
      <td>
        {% if totals.to_refund and totals.to_refund != "0.00" %}
        Excess cash advance — refundable by the accountable officer
        {% elif totals.to_reimburse and totals.to_reimburse != "0.00" %}
        Expenses in excess of the advance — reimbursable to the accountable
        officer
        {% else %}
        Cash advance fully expended — nothing refundable, nothing reimbursable
        {% endif %}
      </td>
      <td class="amount">
        {% if totals.to_refund and totals.to_refund != "0.00" %}
        {{ totals.to_refund | money }}
        {% else %}
        {{ totals.to_reimburse | money }}
        {% endif %}
      </td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Refund of the excess cash advance</h2>
{% if totals.to_refund and totals.to_refund != "0.00" %}
{% if settlement.or_no %}
<table>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>
        Amount refunded per Official Receipt no. {{ settlement.or_no }}
        {% if settlement.or_date %},
        dated {{ settlement.or_date | manila_date }}{% endif %}
      </td>
      <td class="amount">{{ settlement.refund_amount | money }}</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p class="note">
  Settlement recorded {{ settlement.settled_at | manila_datetime }}.
</p>
{% else %}
<p>Official receipt no. ______________________ dated ______________________</p>
<p class="note">
  This copy was produced BEFORE the refund was recorded. COA Circular 97-002
  requires the excess cash advance to be refunded and evidenced by an official
  receipt; the receipt number and date appear on the copy issued once that
  refund is recorded, which supersedes this one.
</p>
{% endif %}
{% else %}
<p class="note">
  Not applicable — no excess cash advance arose on this liquidation.
</p>
{% endif %}

{% if totals.to_reimburse and totals.to_reimburse != "0.00" %}
<h2>Amount reimbursable to the accountable officer</h2>
<p>
  {{ totals.to_reimburse | money }} is due the accountable officer and is
  payable on a separate Disbursement Voucher (GAM Vol. II, Appendix 32).
</p>
{% if settlement.spawned_claim_ref %}
<p class="note">Claimed under reference {{ settlement.spawned_claim_ref }}.</p>
{% else %}
<p class="note">The claim for this difference has not yet been filed.</p>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

<h2>Certifications</h2>
<div class="signature-row">
  <div class="signature-block">
    <p class="signature-role">
      <strong>A. Certified</strong> — correctness of the above data.
    </p>
    <div class="signature-line"></div>
    <p class="signature-name">{{ claimant.full_name }}</p>
    <p class="signature-role">Accountable officer · Date ______________</p>
    {% if certifications.a.recorded_at %}
    <p class="note">
      Filed in Office-Connect
      {{ certifications.a.recorded_at | manila_datetime }}.
    </p>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  <div class="signature-block">
    <p class="signature-role">
      <strong>B. Certified</strong> — purpose of the travel and of the cash
      advance duly accomplished.
    </p>
    <div class="signature-line"></div>
    <p class="signature-name">&nbsp;</p>
    <p class="signature-role">Head of Office · Date ______________</p>
    {% if certifications.b.name %}
    <p class="note">
      Recorded in Office-Connect: certified by {{ certifications.b.name }},
      {{ certifications.b.recorded_at | manila_datetime }}.
    </p>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</div>
<div class="signature-row">
  <div class="signature-block">
    <p class="signature-role">
      <strong>C. Certified</strong> — supporting documents complete and proper.
    </p>
    <div class="signature-line"></div>
    <p class="signature-name">&nbsp;</p>
    <p class="signature-role">Head, Accounting Unit · Date ______________</p>
    {% if certifications.c.recorded_by %}
    <p class="note">
      Recorded in Office-Connect by {{ certifications.c.recorded_by }},
      {{ certifications.c.recorded_at | manila_datetime }}.
      {% if certifications.c.note %}“{{ certifications.c.note }}”{% endif %}
      The signed page is filed under checklist item CRT-C.
    </p>
    {% else %}
    <p class="note">
      To be signed by hand; the signed page is filed under checklist item CRT-C.
    </p>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  <div class="signature-block">
    <p class="signature-role"><strong>For the Accounting Unit</strong></p>
    <div class="signature-line"></div>
    <p class="signature-role">JEV no. ______________ · Date ______________</p>
  </div>
</div>
